# MCP operations

- Check current state before creating resources.
- Avoid duplicate servers, databases, buckets, projects, monitors, workflows, or environments.
- Prefer read operations before mutations when entering a new provider.
- Use environment variables for bearer tokens and API keys.
- Do not print secret values.
- Record provider, resource name, environment, and verification result after a mutation.
- Require explicit owner approval for destructive, production-impacting, or paid operations.
- After mutations, run a health/read-back check instead of assuming success.
